        "summary":  "Kier Group, an 11,000-person UK construction firm, deployed Microsoft 365 Copilot to approximately 40% of staff using a peer-learning \u0027prompt-a-thon\u0027 adoption model to overcome executive resistance. The company is now piloting AI agents for workplace safety data analysis and site monitoring, operating under a \u0027Human at the Helm\u0027 governance philosophy where people maintain control over AI-assisted decisions. The case study highlights change management — not technology — as the primary barrier to enterprise AI adoption.",
        "execSummary":  "Kier Group\u0027s experience reinforces a recurring enterprise AI pattern: the technology is rarely the bottleneck — leadership buy-in and grassroots adoption culture are. The prompt-a-thon peer-learning model is a replicable playbook for organizations facing middle-management resistance to AI tools, particularly in industries where workers are skeptical of automation\u0027s impact on their roles. For support and operations leaders, the safety-monitoring agent use case demonstrates that agentic AI\u0027s highest-value applications in traditional industries are often data synthesis and anomaly detection rather than customer-facing automation. Organizations that invest in adoption culture alongside tool deployment close the gap between license spend and realized productivity faster.",
