        "execSummary":  "Google\u0027s I/O 2026 keynote is a strategic declaration — not just a product launch — that agents are now the primary unit of AI value delivery across every customer segment, signaling that the interface era of AI (chat and search) is giving way to the action era. The Gemini 3.5 Flash cost-performance claim — frontier capability at less than half the price — directly challenges enterprise procurement assumptions and could accelerate token volume growth by making large-scale agent deployments economically viable. For enterprise and customer-support leaders, the trillion-token-per-customer data point signals that the largest enterprises are already operating at a scale where model economics dominate total cost of ownership. The key implication: organizations still in pilot mode risk falling significantly behind peers who are compounding operational efficiency gains at scale.",
