        "summary":  "Google\u0027s Antigravity Teamwork framework — an autonomous multi-agent orchestration system — achieved breakthroughs in theoretical mathematics (seven unsolved problems), systems engineering (a cycle-accurate RISC-V CPU simulator that boots an OS), and open-source optimization by pairing Gemini 3.7 Flash with collaborative agent teams that iterate over hours or days. The system demonstrates that multi-agent architectures, rather than single large-context models, can tackle long-horizon problems that exceed any single agent\u0027s practical scope. Results were published at top research venues including NeurIPS and ICML.",
        "execSummary":  "Google Antigravity\u0027s Teamwork results matter for enterprise leaders not because of the math problems solved, but because they validate the architectural premise that multi-agent orchestration can solve classes of problems that single-agent or single-model approaches cannot. For enterprise AI strategy, this is a signal that long-horizon, multi-step operational problems — complex case resolution, multi-system workflow automation, deep research synthesis — are entering the range of what production agent systems can reliably handle. The RISC-V CPU case demonstrates that agentic systems can now produce outputs requiring precise, verifiable correctness — not just plausible-sounding answers. Decision-makers evaluating agent orchestration platforms should note that Teamwork\u0027s open research publication functions as a capability benchmark against which competing orchestration frameworks will be measured.",
