        "execSummary":  "Production AI agent failures fall into two distinct categories — infrastructure issues and quality degradation — and this framework addresses both, which closes a critical observability gap that most current deployments have. For customer support and operations leaders, the ability to detect when an agent is technically responding but answering incorrectly or incompletely is more valuable than knowing it is up. The autonomous incident investigation capability reduces the mean time to resolution for agent outages by correlating cross-service failures without requiring a human to trace logs manually. Enterprises planning multi-agent rollouts should bake both layers of this monitoring pattern into their operational readiness requirements.",
