        "summary":  "AWS researchers introduced the Agent Evaluation Metric (AEM), a framework for measuring AI agent quality in multi-turn conversations by decomposing performance into sub-metrics like truthfulness and completeness. AEM distinguishes between foundational errors and cascading failures caused by one early mistake corrupting all subsequent turns, allowing teams to identify and fix root causes efficiently. The framework is particularly applicable to customer support automation where conversation quality is critical.",
        "execSummary":  "Aggregate success-rate metrics for conversational AI agents are misleading because a single early error can invalidate an entire interaction and artificially suppress scores. AEM gives customer support and QA teams a turn-level lens that pinpoints exactly which interaction dimension failed — and whether later degradation is a root cause or a symptom — which dramatically accelerates quality improvement cycles. For enterprises deploying AI in customer-facing support channels, this methodology enables SLA-grade quality contracts because failures become attributable and measurable rather than statistical abstractions. Teams should evaluate adopting AEM or equivalent turn-level decomposition as a baseline before scaling any multi-turn support agent to production volume.",
