        "execSummary":  "The emergence of capable local AI models running on RTX and DGX hardware signals that enterprises no longer face a binary choice between cloud AI capability and on-premises data privacy. The hybrid architecture — local models for routine tasks, cloud for complex reasoning — is a viable cost reduction strategy that could materially reduce AI operating expenses for high-volume deployments like customer support. For enterprise IT leaders, the practical implication is that workstation-class hardware purchases may now substitute for a portion of cloud inference spend, which changes the ROI calculus for AI infrastructure investment. Organizations in regulated industries with strict data residency requirements should reprioritize their evaluation of local inference as a deployment path.",
