        "date":  "2026-05-07",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "BNY\u0027s CIO Leigh-Ann Russell describes how \u0027coherence\u0027 — a leadership discipline connecting strategy to execution — helps organizations scale AI without creating chaos. BNY deployed 220 AI solutions and 140 digital employees through a CEO-led strategy, a unified platform called Eliza, and workforce enablement focused on reimagining work around AI. Russell emphasizes balancing talent development, clarity, innovation, and control while avoiding fragmentation across initiatives.",
        "execSummary":  "BNY\u0027s experience offers a replicable model for enterprise leaders: AI scale requires coherence — a top-down strategy that connects every AI deployment back to a single unified platform and a clear workforce narrative. The deployment of 220 AI solutions and 140 digital employees was enabled not by technical excellence alone but by CEO sponsorship, a common platform (Eliza), and employees who understood how their roles would evolve. For customer-support leaders, the lesson is that agentic AI rollouts without coherent governance and workforce alignment create fragmented, ungovernable ecosystems. A unified platform with executive sponsorship is the prerequisite, not the reward, for AI at scale.",
