        "title":  "AI transformation set to shift corporate profits by $4.7 trillion",
        "source":  "CIO Dive",
        "url":  "https://www.ciodive.com/news/AI-transformation-shifting-corporate-profits/829970/",
        "date":  "2026-09-09",
        "theme":  "Strategy",
        "summary":  "Bain \u0026 Co. research indicates AI will transform nearly three-quarters of business sectors by 2035, with $4.7 trillion in profits at stake. Unlike the internet, which reduced distribution costs, AI \u0027collapses the cost of production itself,\u0027 according to the analysis. CIOs are advised to develop proprietary intelligence and focus on innovation rather than general productivity gains, with $3.5 trillion in profit shifts tied to innovation and market dynamics.",
        "execSummary":  "Bain\u0027s $4.7 trillion profit-shift forecast is a clarifying framework for enterprise AI strategy: the companies that capture value will be those that use AI to collapse production costs and drive innovation, not just automate existing workflows. The research distinguishes between productivity gains ($1.2T) and the far larger innovation and market-shift opportunity ($3.5T), suggesting leaders who frame AI primarily as a cost-reduction tool are leaving the majority of the value on the table. For senior customer-support and operations leaders, the strategic implication is to pair efficiency programs with proprietary intelligence development — data assets, models, and workflows competitors cannot easily replicate. Organizations that build proprietary AI capability now will be positioned to capture market share as the profit landscape shifts over the next decade.",
