        "date":  "2026-09-10",
        "theme":  "Agents",
        "summary":  "The article argues that enterprises should prioritize deploying AI agents on their own sites before pursuing broader reach through browser extensions or cloud-based solutions, treating \u0027reach without governance as a liability.\u0027 On-site agents give businesses full control over the model, guardrails, tone, and auditing. The author positions on-site agents as the foundation for future agent-to-agent communication ecosystems.",
        "execSummary":  "The core argument here is a practical sequencing principle for enterprise AI agent deployments: govern your own site first before extending agent reach externally, because external agents creating compliance and security exposure cannot be retrofitted with governance after deployment. For customer-support leaders, this translates into a clear deployment order — internal agent governance, tone, and audit capabilities must be operational before any customer-facing agent goes live at scale. The framing of on-site agents as the foundation for future agent-to-agent ecosystems is also strategically important: organizations that build governed on-site agents now are positioning themselves for the multi-agent orchestration landscape that is emerging. The caveat is that \u0027on-site first\u0027 may delay competitive deployment windows if competitors move faster with less governance.",
